    "narrative": "The cornerstone of today\u2019s lineup is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who at an 81.07 score remains our premier asset. His matchup against Singer is bolstered by elite BvP data (+8%) and a favorable order placement, making him a locked-in must-start. **Cal Raleigh** (76.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (72.31) follow closely, both benefiting from dynamic platoon edges against Lauer and Littell, respectively. These three represent the core of our daily offensive floor, providing the power profile required to remain competitive in Roto categories while maintaining high efficiency.\n\nWe are keeping a close watch on **Gleyber Torres** (67.52), whose projection has surged thanks to an ideal platoon pairing against Rogers and a leadoff slot that maximizes his counting stat potential. Conversely, our toughest start is **Masyn Winn** (46.74); while he provides a necessary speed element, he is neutralized by a difficult matchup against Boyd. The most difficult bench decision involved **Gavin Sheets** (45.14), who narrowly missed the starting cut. Despite a positive platoon advantage against Hughes, his lower raw efficiency compared to **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Tyler Freeman** forced him to the bench to preserve our limited game caps. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the current board. **Taylor Ward** is facing the formidable Skubal; while his platoon edge keeps him relevant, his 53.36 score is largely buoyed by order placement, making him a volatile piece in the outfield. Furthermore, **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh** rely on assumed lineup positions; should these shift during official posting, their expected efficiency may fluctuate. We are opting to bench **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Braden Montgomery** entirely, as their sub-40 scores against elite pitching indicate a high risk of negative impact on our season-long averages.",
